      "writtenOn": "2018-12-26T11:49:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Actually shared_buf and shared_buffer are not the same thing. The name is not descriptive.\nshare_buf element size in the ipc_share_obj, and shared_buffer is the 296*2 byte starting address shared between AP and SCP.\n\nstruct ipc_share_obj {                                \n        /* IPC ID */                                  \n        int32_t id;                                   \n        /* Length of the contents in share_buf. */    \n        uint32_t len;                                 \n        /* Share buffer contents. */                  \n        uint8_t share_buf[CONFIG_IPC_SHARE_BUF_SIZE]; \n};                                                    \n\nRenames to CONFIG_IPC_SHARED_OBJ_ADDR",
